  "notes": "A self-contained band playing bluegrass-derived precision inside radio country — \"the tightest ensemble playing in the section.\" The entry's one explicit engine instruction is the humanize block: \"Playing is quantise-tight by hand — model very low timing variance and near-zero velocity drift,\" so `quantizeStrength` sits at 0.98 with `velocityVar` at 0.04 and single-millisecond jitter, which is the tightest reading anywhere in this batch. Harmony is the stated \"I–IV–V, I–♭VII–IV, and quick-cycling I–V–vi–IV on the ballads,\" with the ♭VII coming from the mixolydian colour the entry attributes to the string instruments. The bass is quoted: \"locked to the kick with fast, articulate root-fifth-octave motion on the uptempo cuts; the bass frequently plays a written line rather than a pattern,\" hence `mirror_kick` with a root-fifth-octave cell set rather than the genre's boom-chick. The countermelody carries the band's identity — \"mandolin, banjo-adjacent picking, fiddle, pedal steel and Tele all take short 2-bar answers in rotation\" — which is the highest answer-lick density in this batch. ⚠ Boundary flag: the fast catalogue is train-beat and two-beat driven and those grooves belong to `country-train`. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high) and the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the counter density ratio and the perc lane set.",
